  "text": "                                        Kaushley Mehra\\n                         Technical Product Manager — Supply Chain & Optimization Systems\\n                                     91-9899225890 | kaushley14@gmail.com | LinkedIn\\n\\nSummary\\n Technical product manager who owns and personally builds the decision logic inside India’s largest quick-commerce\\n replenishment system — storage, reverse logistics, and inventory health across 2,500+ dark stores. Ships the optimization and\\n statistical models directly (Python, SQL, linear programming, empirical Bayes) rather than specifying them. Previously employee\\n #4 at a beverage-commerce startup, building operations, full-stack systems, and a new revenue line from zero.\\n\\nProfessional Experience\\n Product Manager – Replenishment                                                                       August 2024 – Present\\n Blinkit (Eternal Company)                                                                                       Gurugram, HR\\n\\n   – Own the replenishment decision logic — storage-aware allocation, reverse stock transfers (RSTOs), and inventory\\n     health — within the autonomous replenishment system (ARS) serving 2,500+ dark stores through a 3.5x scale-up.\\n   – Diagnosed storage constraints as the largest driver of availability loss (50–64% of unit drops in peak months; INR\\n     160–750 Cr/month GMV at risk); designed an opportunity-cost–based RSTO cost function closing the missing\\n     feedback loop between storage truncation and reverse-transfer creation — +72% RSTO share at storage-constrained\\n     stores (18% → 31.6%) and –26% damage-prone RSTO creation, from single-warehouse pilot to network rollout.\\n   – Architected and personally coded the translation layer between digitized on-ground store layouts and ARS, moving\\n     storage truncation from static item-tag rules to live on-shelf-utilization signals — eliminating recurring manual inputs\\n     and avoiding a severe system rewrite.\\n   – Replaced ad-hoc reverse-transfer clearance with a tiered, least-aggressive-first escalation framework triggered strictly\\n     on storage conditions and linked to assortment states, festive modes, and throttleable configuration — raising RSTO\\n     automation from ˜56% to 90–95% across ˜30x volume growth (0.4M → 11–13M units/month).\\n   – Designed and coded a city-scale dead-inventory reclassification engine (Bengaluru, 3M+ item-outlet pairs):\\n     exposure-adjusted staleness, per-category p80 cutoffs, velocity-based item immunity, and empirical-Bayes item effects —\\n     replacing blunt legacy dead flags with statistically defensible, category-relative signals.\\n   – Contributed to a +450 bps store-level availability gain (p50 74% → 79%) via the allocation-logic and clearance changes,\\n     sustained through ˜9x peak-demand events with near-zero manual overrides.\\n\\n Founding Team Member                                                                                June 2022 – August 2024\\n Sip Direct (Ontap Direct Private Limited)                                                                      Bangalore, KT\\n Beverage commerce platform | 4 cities | 350+ pincodes | 50k+ orders delivered\\n\\n   – Joined as employee #4, before product or operational systems existed — set up and optimized the foundational loops\\n     across operations, technology, finance, and analytics, and stayed the person pulled into urgent, undefined problems.\\n   – Built a net-new high-margin revenue stream (Bartending-as-a-Service) from idea to first order — partner onboarding,\\n     tech/product implementation, SOPs — eventually contributing 25% of company earnings.\\n   – Autonomously launched Siliguri operations end to end in ˜60 days — onboarded retailers, delivery partners, and\\n     feet-on-ground, localized the GTM — the company’s 2nd operational city, growing to ˜20% of company GMV.\\n   – Worked as a full-stack developer on the core engineering team — React/Node, Apollo GraphQL BFF, Prisma\\n     ORM, MySQL in a microservices stack — wrote the first line of code in multiple repos, building internal operations\\n     tooling and the consumer app, while interim-running scrums, roadmap, tech debt, and backlog.\\n   – Owned the data and reporting stack — schemas, dashboards, and data architecture across 7+ applications — and ran\\n     the platform’s first 3 sales-enablement campaigns for a major alcobev brand.\\n\\nEducation\\n Birla Institute of Technology and Science, Pilani                                                      July 2018 – June 2023\\n Bachelor of Engineering in Mechanical Engineering\\n Master of Science in Chemistry (dual degree)\\n\\nSkills\\n Modeling & Data: Python, SQL, Linear Programming (PuLP), Statistical Modeling (Empirical-Bayes Shrinkage), Airflow\\n Engineering: React, Node.js, Apollo GraphQL, Prisma ORM, MySQL, Microservices\\n Domain: Demand Forecasting, Inventory Optimization, Reverse Logistics, Storage & Capacity Planning, Dead-Stock\\n Classification, Data Architecture & Reporting\\n\\f"
